--------------------------------

    Docker Commands Notes

--------------------------------

1. Check Docker Version

docker --version

Shows the installed Docker version.

Example:

Docker version 28.x.x

--------------------------------

2. Check Docker Service Status

systemctl status docker

Checks whether Docker service is running or not.

-------------------------------------

3. Add User to Docker Group

sudo usermod -aG docker sachin

Allows user "sachin" to run Docker commands without sudo.

--------------------------------------------

Basic Docker Commands

4. Run Nginx Container

docker run nginx

Pulls nginx image (if not available), creates a container, and starts it.

----------------------------------------------

5. Run Container in Background

docker run -d nginx

-d = Detached Mode (runs in background).

----------------------------------------------

6. List Running Containers

docker ps

Shows only running containers.

------------------------------------

7. List All Containers

docker ps -a

Shows running and stopped containers.

---------------------------------------

8. Show Only Container IDs

docker ps -aq

Displays only container IDs.

----------------------------------------

9. Inspect Container Details

docker inspect <container-id>

Shows detailed information about a container.

--------------------------------------------

10. Run Container with Port Mapping

docker run -p 80:80 -d nginx

Maps host port 80 to container port 80.

Format:

docker run -p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT IMAGE

-----------------------------------------

11. Publish All Ports

docker run -P -d nginx

Docker automatically assigns available host ports.

-----------------------------------------

12. View Linux Processes

ps -elf

Displays all running processes in Linux.

--------------------------------------------

Docker Run Process

docker run
   ↓
Pull Image
   ↓
Create Container
   ↓
Start Container

Docker Run = Pull + Create + Start

-------------------------------------------

Container Management

13. Stop Container

docker stop <container-id>

Stops a running container.

------------------------------------------

14. Start Container

docker start <container-id>

Starts a stopped container.

-----------------------------------------

15. Check Containers

docker ps -a

View all containers.

------------------------------------

Delete Container

16. Remove Container

docker rm <container-id>

Deletes a stopped container.

----------------------------------------

17. Force Remove Container

docker rm -f <container-id>

Stops and deletes container immediately.

-------------------------------------------

Access Container

18. Login to Container

docker exec -it <container-id> bash

Opens terminal inside container.

Options:

- i = Interactive
- t = Terminal

Exit:

exit

--------------------------------------------

Copy Files

19. Copy File to Container

docker cp file.txt <container-id>:/tmp

Copies file from host to container.

-------------------------------------------

Logs

20. View Container Logs

docker logs <container-id>

Shows container logs.

--------------------------------------

21. Follow Logs Live

docker logs -f <container-id>

Displays logs in real time.

-------------------------------------

Resource Usage

22. Container Statistics

docker container stats

Shows CPU, Memory, and Network usage.

Single container:

docker container stats <container-id>

----------------------------------------

Docker Images

23. List Images

docker images

Shows downloaded images.

----------------------------------------

24. Delete Image

docker rmi <image-id>

Removes an image.

Note:
Delete containers first, then delete images.

-----------------------------------------

Download Images

25. Pull Apache Image

docker pull httpd

Downloads Apache image.

------------------------------------------

26. Pull Any Image

docker pull <image-name>

Example:

docker pull nginx
docker pull ubuntu
docker pull redis

-----------------------------------------

Search Images

27. Search Docker Hub Images

docker search nginx

or

docker search netflix

Searches images available on Docker Hub.
